# Credentials & session state — NEVER commit
auth.json
auth_state.json
asana_auth_state.json

# Secrets — real credential values live in .env. NEVER commit it.
# The .env.template (no values, safe) IS tracked so teammates know the keys.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.template

# Client data — invoices, queue, run logs
*.xlsx
invoices/

# Debug & test screenshots (may contain client data)
debug_*.png
test_row_*.png

# Page-structure dumps from diagnose_section_structure.py.
# These capture whatever was on screen in Asana -- real vendor names,
# LLCs, invoice numbers and amounts. The script writes them to THIS
# folder (see diagnose_section_structure.py, OUT_FILE); we file them
# under debug-logs/ afterwards, so both locations are blocked.
*_section-structure-dump.txt

# Output of diagnose_vendor_dropdown.py -- the text and screenshot hold what
# Rent Manager's vendor suggestion list showed (real vendor names).
*_vendor-dropdown-dump.txt
*_vendor-dropdown-dump.png

# The WHOLE debug-logs folder. Everything in here is a record of a real run,
# so any file type in it can hold real vendor names, LLCs, invoice numbers
# and amounts -- not just the .txt and .png we used to block. Blocking the
# folder means a new kind of log file can never leak by being an extension
# nobody thought of.
debug-logs/

# Per-machine settings (shared drive path, Mac IP) -- never commit
config.json

# Per-PC reader settings (holds the Mac's address). The .template is tracked.
reader_settings.bat

# Virtual environment (created by Setup.bat, machine-specific)
venv/

# Throwaway staging folder for copying files to the Mac. It holds COPIES of
# tracked scripts -- committing it would put the same code in the repo twice.
mac-bundle/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Office temp/lock files
~$*

# OCR output & logs (contain client invoice text)
Tesseract_Testing/*.txt
Tesseract_Testing/*.log

# Cloned third-party repo
Tesseract_Testing/poppler-windows/

# Claude Code tool-call transcripts -- record every command run, with
# machine paths, and can end up describing real client data indirectly.
.claude/logs/*.log

# Run logs written inside the project folder (diagnose_scroll_loading.py
# writes its screen output here when the Z: drive is not used). They hold
# real vendor and task names.
run-logs/

# Output of diagnose_scroll_loading.py. Older runs wrote it to the project
# root. It holds real task names.
*_scroll-loading-dump.txt

# Output of diagnose_asana_fields.py. It normally writes into debug-logs/
# (already blocked above), but older runs wrote to the project root. It
# holds real property names, unit numbers and invoice amounts.
*_asana-fields.txt
*_asana-fields.png

# Cross-tool agent config (Codex / Antigravity / Gemini CLI). Kept out of
# git on purpose -- it is per-machine scaffolding and may reference local
# MCP endpoints, paths and connectors. Mirror of .claude/ for other tools.
.agents/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-11-13 during the setup audit. Each of these was verified with
# `git check-ignore -v` beforehand and was NOT being ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The SQLite database. It holds real vendor names, property names, invoice
# numbers and amounts -- the single most sensitive file in the project. It is
# also large and changes every run, so committing it would bloat history and
# leak client data at the same time. Keep it OUTSIDE the repo entirely.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Superpowers working folder -- brainstorm output, draft plans and UI mockups
# land here automatically. Scratch material, not a deliverable. Anything worth
# keeping gets written to docs/ by hand.
.superpowers/

# The retired handoff system (replaced 2026-11-13 by context/HOTcontext.md,
# written by /session-end). The old notes quote real run output, so they stay
# out of git even while the folder is still sitting on disk.
handoffs/

# Backup copies made before an edit. Git is the backup now; these are clutter
# and they duplicate whatever secret the original held.
*.bak
*.bak-*

# Per-project Claude settings: Headroom routing and local hook paths.
# NOTE: this was previously ignored ONLY by the machine-global ignore file
# (C:\Users\<you>\.config\git\ignore), so a fresh clone on another PC would
# have started tracking it. Pinning the rule here makes it travel with the repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
